 16 of 318's 23 events occur after that point. In the single overlapping period, 318's out-partners (259,652,1162,1528) are disjoint from 480's entire 1-hop neighbourhood (149,229,544,734,848,935,972,1791), and 600-unit binning shows only isolated, non-chained single events. No sequence of interactions with consecutive gaps <= 600 can carry influence from 318 to 480."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoints exist but are temporally segregated.**\n\n- Both nodes are active in the window (318: 23 events, 480: 20 events; step_02), and a static connection exists at \u22653 hops \u2014 but 318's out\u2011neighbourhood {250,259,409,436,603,652,735,861,987,1035,1140,1162,1329,1342,1407,1528,1673,1778,1988} (step_03) and 480's in\u2011neighbourhood {102,149,229,243,334,544,762,817,848,972,1114,1150,1214,1387,1600,1624,1791,1821} (step_04) are **disjoint** \u2014 no 1\u2011 or 2\u2011hop hand\u2011off.\n- **Timing is the decisive problem.** 480's events are front\u2011loaded: 10 / 4 / 1 / 3 / 1 / 1 / **0** / **0** across the eight sub\u2011windows (step_09) \u2014 it is completely silent after t\u224843621. 318 is back\u2011loaded: 0 / 2 / 0 / 1 / 2 / 2 / **8** / **8** (step_07, step_08). The bulk of 318's activity (16 of 23 events) occurs *after* 480 has stopped receiving anything, so it cannot seed any chain into 480.\n- In the only overlapping period [22022, 41221], 318 emits to just 4 partners (259, 652, 1162, 1528; step_12), while 480's entire 1\u2011hop neighbourhood is the 8 nodes {149,229,544,734,848,935,972,1791} (step_13) \u2014 again disjoint, so a chain would need \u22653 intermediate hops each within 600 units.\n- Fine\u2011grained 600\u2011unit binning of that overlap shows 318 and 480 each fire only isolated single events (step_15, step_16): 318 at [34022,34621] and [40022,40621]; 480 at [34022,34621] and [38822,39421]. The one co\u2011occupied 600\u2011bin cannot host a \u22653\u2011hop relay in the required direction, and the other bins are separated by >600 with no intervening relay structure.\n- The 2\u2011hop and 3\u2011hop expansions (step_05, step_06, step_14) confirm the two neighbourhoods only merge through very high\u2011degree hubs (81, 302, 511, 733, 734) \u2014 a static-connectivity artefact of hub popularity, not a timed relay; this is the confounder that \"connection when time is ignored\" would falsely suggest.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_fd7e502f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [318, 480],\n  \"window\": [14821, 53221],\n  \"confidence\": 0.79,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"318 and 480 are both active and are weakly connected when time is ignored, but only via high-degree hubs (81/302/511/733/734) at 3+ hops. Temporally the two are anti-phased: 480 receives all of its traffic early and is silent after t=43621, whereas 16 of 318's 23 events occur after that point. In the single overlapping period, 318's out-partners (259,652,1162,1528) are disjoint from 480's entire 1-hop neighbourhood (149,229,544,734,848,935,972,1791), and 600-unit binning shows only isolated, non-chained single events. No sequence of interactions with consecutive gaps <= 600 can carry influence from 318 to 480.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 72169, "total_output_tokens": 10015, "total_tokens": 82184, "total_latency_ms": 151079, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}